    {
      "short": "Scale out",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "title": "Horizontal scaling & load balancing",
      "body": [
        "One big server has a ceiling; many small servers don't. A <span class=\"term\">load balancer</span> spreads requests across N instances and — critically — health-checks them, so a crashed instance is pulled from rotation in seconds.",
        "Kubernetes adds <span class=\"term\">autoscaling</span>: pods scale with load. A <span class=\"term\">CDN</span> absorbed your static traffic (photos!) at the edge — half your read load never touched your servers at all."
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "insight",
        "text": "Scale-up takes minutes (metrics → scheduling → image pull → warm), so sudden spikes still hurt before new pods arrive."
      },
