    {
      "short": "Scale-out cost",
      "chapter": "tradeoff",
      "title": "Horizontal scaling isn't a checkbox",
      "body": [
        "Horizontal scaling requires <span class=\"term\">stateless services</span> — state pushed down to DB/cache. That's an architecture decision, not a checkbox.",
        "Autoscaling trades cost-efficiency for spike-vulnerability. For predictable launches: pre-scale. More instances = more things to observe, deploy, and debug — the LB is now critical infrastructure."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "+ CDN for static reads",
        "+ Load Balancer + K8s Cluster (replaces single API server)",
        "~ Static reads now never touch your origin"
      ],
